1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,180
Music by Ryan . . .

2
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:18,280
.

3
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:26,180
BIRDS CHIRP

4
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:55,840
Oh, my God.

5
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:19,110
Ah!

6
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:22,210
Ah!

7
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:24,190
Ah!

8
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:33,940
Hell Fist!

9
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:37,280
Junction! Hell Fist! Hell Fist!

10
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:42,660
Hell Fist!

11
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:16,240
I'll be back with you.

12
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:17,897
I'll be back with you.

13
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:21,400
All of us, we're going
to be back with you.

14
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:28,060
I won't be able to fight you.

15
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:33,260
There's no way we can fight you.

16
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:38,440
I'll be back with you.

17
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:41,620
You'll be back with us.

18
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:06,300
How is that possible?

19
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,442
They left Garp on Pirate Island?

20
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:09,657
What happened to him?

21
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:13,037
The article says he went there
to rescue some guy named Kobe.

22
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,560
I guess he succeeded.

23
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:16,297
Too bad it cost him his life.

24
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:18,027
Where does it say he's dead?

25
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:19,657
The man's a living legend.

26
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:21,397
This isn't how he's gonna go.

27
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:23,877
I push looks off your faces. You're right.

28
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,078
I'm sure he's fine.

29
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:26,780
Damn right he is.

30
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:30,680
Who's laughing?

31
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:32,332
You think this is funny?

32
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:35,760
Oh, sweetheart.

33
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:37,350
Don't worry.

34
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:38,559
He didn't mean it.

35
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:39,510
There, there.

36
00:03:39,740 --> 00:03:41,340
Oh, it was just the baby.

37
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:42,758
I'm sorry, Machado.

38
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:45,611
You're worried about Garp too, aren't you?

39
00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:47,797
Was that what you were laughing at?

40
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:50,056
You know Luffy's face now, don't you?

41
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:52,200
We love Luffy. Yes, we do.

42
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,353
What the hell are those idiots thinking?

43
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:18,000
Oh, we've got a big one!

44
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:24,060
It's an earthquake!

45
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:34,320
It's a tsunami!

46
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:36,620
It's a heartbreak!

47
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:39,060
Follow me!

48
00:04:47,980 --> 00:04:52,620
The earthquake on that day was
unlike any other in recorded history.

49
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:56,740
It caused devastating
damage all around the world.

50
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:11,200
We're too late!

51
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:19,300
The situation was highly unusual.

52
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:22,417
The earthquake's epicenter
could not be detected.

53
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:24,676
The truth was hidden from the public.

54
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:28,237
But it was no coincidence that the
tragedy occurred six days after

55
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:31,977
the kingdom of Lucia was wiped off
the map by the world government.

56
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:33,720
I'm at the remains of Lucia!

57
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:36,077
There is no trace of the land anymore!

58
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:38,860
Just a giant hole swallowing up the sea!

59
00:05:39,060 --> 00:05:41,280
No further approach is possible!

60
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:42,913
The hole isn't milling!

61
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:46,800
Across the entire world,

62
00:05:47,020 --> 00:05:51,900
sea levels rose by approximately one meter
following the havoc of the earthquake.

63
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:56,260
The beach has never flooded like this!

64
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:03,857
At this rate, there won't be
any beach left here at all!

65
00:06:03,940 --> 00:06:05,677
Why isn't the tide pulling back?

66
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:07,500
This is too cruel!

67
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:11,440
Running on the beach is
our favorite pastime!

68
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,540
Give it back!

69
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:17,360
This isn't glamorous at all!

70
00:06:18,140 --> 00:06:23,520
A number of beaches have disappeared from
the world, along with several islands.

71
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:28,080
There's nothing left for us here.

72
00:06:28,220 --> 00:06:29,080
We have to go!

73
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:31,580
My shark swim right into my house!

74
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:35,517
It's not supposed to be high tide yet.

75
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:37,659
Might make for a big catch, though.

76
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:40,289
You really want to go
sailing in this mess?

77
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:45,232
Sir, an update on the flooding situation.

78
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:48,740
Sea levels are rising around the world.

79
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:51,580
Yes, sir, but the cause is unclear.

80
00:06:53,740 --> 00:06:58,780
Meanwhile, Egghead was surrounded by a
fleet of 100 Navy vessels of various sizes,

81
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,080
including 20 massive battleships.

82
00:07:01,580 --> 00:07:03,797
This was a force that
could level a nation,

83
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:06,960
with power far exceeding
even that of a Buster Call.

84
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:11,600
The total number of Marines was 30,000.

85
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:15,500
And the leaders of this
unprecedented operation...

86
00:07:21,580 --> 00:07:24,460
...were nine Navy HQ vice-amirals.

87
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:32,700
and Admiral Chizuru.

88
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:37,640
We're under attack!

89
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:18,700
Hey, I told you not to
attack the sea-beast weapons!

90
00:08:19,260 --> 00:08:22,780
I heard you, but I'm
afraid to detect us first.

91
00:08:24,740 --> 00:08:26,269
Your milk, he's over, sir.

92
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:29,780
Oh, my favorite.

93
00:08:30,840 --> 00:08:31,700
There you go.

94
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:33,234
Eat it while it's hot.

95
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:37,410
Mmm.

96
00:08:38,700 --> 00:08:39,530
Huh?

97
00:08:40,580 --> 00:08:44,815
I gotta say, you're really putting
me on the spot here, you said tomato.

98
00:08:46,060 --> 00:08:50,001
Why don't you just surrender and
have a nice bowl of ramen with me?

99
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:50,950
Get serious.

100
00:08:51,260 --> 00:08:53,201
Attack again and we'll open fire.

101
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:55,797
Ooh, now you're scaring me.

102
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:57,797
You know what you're up against here.

103
00:08:57,880 --> 00:09:01,468
Punk developed the pacifista's
lasers by studying your power.

104
00:09:02,140 --> 00:09:03,520
Wow, so cool!

105
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:07,445
Now you're here to murder him.

106
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:09,757
Never thought things
would turn out this way.

107
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:12,240
He studied the void century, Sentomaru.

108
00:09:12,540 --> 00:09:15,599
Old friend or not, I can't
defend a crime like that.

109
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:19,500
In the end, I'm just the Navy's puppet.

110
00:09:21,140 --> 00:09:24,577
That said we don't want to have
this battle any more than you do.

111
00:09:24,660 --> 00:09:27,437
The more we destroy the more we lose.

112
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:33,097
I was really hoping Luchi would clean this
up quickly without trashing the place.

113
00:09:33,180 --> 00:09:35,651
You can thank the Straw Hats for that one.

114
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:43,057
Don't let anyone else know I'm here.

115
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:44,097
Yes sir.

116
00:09:44,180 --> 00:09:47,277
The Straw Hats took Vagabond hostage.

117
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:49,420
and barricaded themselves inside.

118
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:51,460
I like this article.

119
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:53,540
It's Morgan's work.

120
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,540
And what is the truth?

121
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:59,841
Sir, we haven't received word that
CP0 has completed their mission.

122
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:03,700
Sentumatu is prepared to
defend the island outside,

123
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:06,574
so we can guess who's in the labophase.

124
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:08,200
First, we have Dr.

125
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:10,673
Vegapunk, along with his six satellites.

126
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:14,200
They should have the Four
Seraphim protecting them.

127
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:19,482
Then there's Straw Hat Luffy and his crew,
who seem to have allied with the Doctor.

128
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:23,130
Also,

129
00:10:23,213 --> 00:10:28,100
there's CP-0's Wabluci, along with the
others in his leading unit, Kaku and Stussy.

130
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:31,179
As for the other Cypherpole agents,

131
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:33,197
they appear to have been
captured by Sentomaru

132
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:35,574
and his pacifistas in the Fabrio phase.

133
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:38,520
One added note.

134
00:10:39,460 --> 00:10:42,837
The Frontier Dome's barrier
status is currently at 100%,

135
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:46,096
meaning that no one can enter
or leave the Lobby phase.

136
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:48,535
It's been like that for an entire day.

137
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:51,309
We still don't know
what's going on inside.

138
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:54,657
What happened to all
the research staff and

139
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:57,180
technicians who were employed on Egghead?

140
00:10:57,940 --> 00:10:59,116
They're not present.

141
00:10:59,280 --> 00:11:01,377
They evacuated the island yesterday.

142
00:11:01,460 --> 00:11:03,377
We've already located their ships.

143
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:05,660
And what if they know too much?

144
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:08,380
Sink them at once.

145
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:09,520
Yes, sir.

146
00:11:10,260 --> 00:11:11,820
Just one more thing first.

147
00:11:12,260 --> 00:11:13,940
We spotted Jewelry Bonnie.

148
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:16,396
She may be there with the Straw Hats.

149
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:18,631
Kuma's daughter, you say?

150
00:11:18,780 --> 00:11:20,900
We have no more use for her.

151
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:22,600
Forget about her.

152
00:11:22,860 --> 00:11:24,140
She's just a girl.

153
00:11:24,660 --> 00:11:25,490
Yes, sir.

154
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:29,820
Admiral, sir!

155
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:32,910
What?

156
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:35,800
I'm trying to enjoy a meal here.

157
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,237
We're picking up a signal
coming from Egghead.

158
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:39,150
A signal.

159
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:41,697
They seem to be making a call somewhere.

160
00:11:41,780 --> 00:11:44,133
We'll find out who they're calling then.

161
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:49,920
It's Marie Joie!

162
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:56,320
Who is this?

163
00:11:57,400 --> 00:12:01,077
Admiral, you should have a black
transponder snail on your wrist.

164
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:01,990
Oh.

165
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:03,595
You can tap the call.

166
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:04,870
Whoa.

167
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:16,100
Yeah, hello, it's me! York!

168
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:17,920
You're still alive.

169
00:12:18,260 --> 00:12:19,777
That's all you have to say?

170
00:12:19,860 --> 00:12:21,197
Are you Pangaea kidding me?

171
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:23,417
What the hell are you
trying to kill me, too?

172
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:25,857
I'm the one who told you what Stella did.

173
00:12:25,940 --> 00:12:27,293
Remember that, Pops?

174
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:32,060
Be that as it may, you're still
a Vegapunk, just like the others.

175
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:34,937
I don't give a shit
about the Void Century.

176
00:12:35,020 --> 00:12:38,902
And even if I did, you think I
would have tipped you off about it?

177
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:39,850
You debate!

178
00:12:41,700 --> 00:12:42,640
Fair enough.

179
00:12:43,140 --> 00:12:44,760
But how did you survive?

180
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:47,260
Did CP0 fail at their mission?

181
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:50,120
And what is the status of the Straw Hats?

182
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:54,280
Well, I'm still here.

183
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:57,266
That alone should tell
you how the others are.

184
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:59,800
I'm no one calling the shots now.

185
00:13:00,940 --> 00:13:02,620
An egghead is mine.

186
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:04,140
All mine.

187
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:07,620
You know what that means?

188
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:13,537
If your skin bags try to
backstab me again, I call...

189
00:13:13,620 --> 00:13:15,400
The Big Guns!

190
00:13:20,620 --> 00:13:22,460
Oh, for Seraphim.

191
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:26,090
Now...

192
00:13:26,173 --> 00:13:29,000
About your little fleet
surrounding the island.

193
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:32,165
You trying to start a
war with me or something?

194
00:13:32,660 --> 00:13:35,500
We could be convinced to
alter our plans, York.

195
00:13:37,020 --> 00:13:39,160
But let me confirm one thing first.

196
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:41,872
Can you create the Mother Flame yourself?

197
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:49,340
Oh, now they want to negotiate.

198
00:13:49,740 --> 00:13:51,622
I'm glad I sent you that sample.

199
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:54,407
I knew you'd get hooked
once you had a piece.

200
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:56,800
It is of the highest priority.

201
00:13:57,680 --> 00:13:59,357
Whose priority, I wonder?

202
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:02,793
Too bad this island's the only
power plant that makes it.

203
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,260
Here's the sitch.

204
00:14:14,860 --> 00:14:19,260
Promise that me and the lab will
make it out of this thing unscathed.

205
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:20,930
Agreed.

206
00:14:21,220 --> 00:14:23,657
And make me a celestial
dragon while you're at it.

207
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:24,760
It shall be done.

208
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:27,940
Then we've got ourselves a deal.

209
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:30,080
One more thing.

210
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:34,220
I need you to come and save me!

211
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:36,940
Straw Luffy is here!

212
00:14:37,300 --> 00:14:39,400
And he's gonna kill me!

213
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:42,080
What? What's this?

214
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:43,791
What's going on in there?

215
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:48,000
Hey, Luffy.

216
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:50,482
What should we do with this one?

217
00:14:50,660 --> 00:14:53,220
No more use for her now, right? No!

218
00:14:54,980 --> 00:14:59,080
Spass them all dead! No!
No! Do it now! Please!

219
00:15:00,140 --> 00:15:02,080
What a disaster this has been.

220
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:04,940
I've caused you all such trouble. Sorry.

221
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,400
Eh, we forgive you.

222
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:08,380
But she is a different story.

223
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:11,140
So, Luffy, what's the plan for her?

224
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:14,800
They wanna keep her alive, right?

225
00:15:15,540 --> 00:15:18,069
Let's use her as a
shield when we run away.

226
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:20,454
So, it's like a hostage situation, huh?

227
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,141
Talk to me, Doc.

228
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:23,297
She gonna be okay?

229
00:15:23,380 --> 00:15:28,086
It'll take time for her wounds to heal,
but with plenty of rest, she'll be fine.

230
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:31,370
Hello!

231
00:15:32,660 --> 00:15:33,490
Huh?

232
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:36,780
My name is Monkey D.

233
00:15:37,100 --> 00:15:39,960
Luffy, and I'm gonna
be king of the pirates!

234
00:15:40,220 --> 00:15:41,317
That's what you choose to open with?

235
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:42,737
What is wrong with you?

236
00:15:42,820 --> 00:15:43,920
We have Dr.

237
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:46,437
Vegapunk, all the Vegapunks even!

238
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:53,377
If you want to save York's life, clear
your ships from the shore, every last one.

239
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:55,180
You don't understand.

240
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:05,617
What is he doing?

241
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:08,137
No, Luffy? Why?

242
00:16:08,220 --> 00:16:09,797
That story was fake.

243
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:12,297
So you're Straw Hat Luffy? Are you?

244
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:15,220
Have you suffered any
casualties in the lab?

245
00:16:15,380 --> 00:16:17,027
Who is still there with you?

246
00:16:18,860 --> 00:16:20,400
Well, uh, let me see.

247
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:22,207
A couple of people are hurt.

248
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:26,210
Kali.

249
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:28,120
A woman's voice.

250
00:16:28,740 --> 00:16:30,260
Must be Nico Robin.

251
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:32,609
Why'd you make me hang up?

252
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:33,940
Intel is a weapon.

253
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:36,814
You must never give it to your enemies.

254
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:38,520
Oh, right. Sorry.

255
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:40,897
But hey, the ships will be gone now.

256
00:16:40,980 --> 00:16:42,460
What the hell they will?

257
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:44,580
You think the Navy's that dumb?

258
00:16:46,940 --> 00:16:48,320
What's our next move?

259
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:50,854
There are three things we must protect.

260
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:55,360
York's safety, the data
stored inside punk records,

261
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:58,800
and the power plant that
creates the Mother Flame.

262
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:01,660
Everything else is expendable.

263
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:07,617
But sir, Rob Lucci and the other Cypherpole
agents are still trapped inside there.

264
00:17:07,700 --> 00:17:09,657
We might face a worst-case scenario.

265
00:17:09,740 --> 00:17:12,497
We must prioritize accordingly.

266
00:17:12,580 --> 00:17:18,097
regard humans as you
regard insects even if

267
00:17:18,180 --> 00:17:20,800
you exterminate some
they'll multiply again!

268
00:17:26,140 --> 00:17:30,317
Yes sir you listen to
me you tiny terrorists

269
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:33,177
I need a pact with the five elders you get

270
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:36,297
it hurt me and you die
what they do to this

271
00:17:36,380 --> 00:17:38,909
island will make Uhura
look like fireworks!

272
00:17:49,060 --> 00:17:50,140
That hurt!

273
00:17:51,180 --> 00:17:52,460
You're gonna pay!

274
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:54,661
I'll sic the elders on you first!

275
00:17:54,940 --> 00:17:55,770
Yeah?

276
00:17:55,853 --> 00:17:56,683
Go right ahead!

277
00:17:57,020 --> 00:17:58,857
You're lucky that's all you got!

278
00:17:58,940 --> 00:18:00,817
How dare you say that in front of Robin!

279
00:18:00,900 --> 00:18:02,960
Keep your filthy mouth shut!

280
00:18:03,540 --> 00:18:05,017
She can't hurt us.

281
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:06,160
Just ignore her.

282
00:18:07,180 --> 00:18:10,600
Robin are you feeling okay? Of course.

283
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:12,233
Have you met my doctor?

284
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:13,230
He's brilliant

285
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:21,820
Pretty pathetic display though to be fair.

286
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:24,159
I was fighting to Sarah him at once

287
00:18:26,300 --> 00:18:27,840
You need to rest

288
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:39,120
Oh, my God!

289
00:18:41,420 --> 00:18:43,244
Could you quiet down for a sec?

290
00:18:43,340 --> 00:18:44,170
What?

291
00:18:44,253 --> 00:18:47,093
I'm trying to get in contact
with the basement right now.

292
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:50,429
Hey, can you guys hear me?

293
00:18:50,540 --> 00:18:51,893
Everyone's still alive?

294
00:18:52,520 --> 00:18:53,880
Thank you, Straw Hats!

295
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:57,780
We can finally eat again!

296
00:18:58,080 --> 00:18:59,220
You saved us!

297
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:00,640
We were losing hope!

298
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:02,757
So good!

299
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:03,860
I'm alive!

300
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:08,640
Man, do I love the Straw Hat crew!

301
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:10,174
That's so loud, buddy.

302
00:19:10,540 --> 00:19:11,716
We're still enemies.

303
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,617
Now, is there any chance you
could let us out of this room?

304
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:18,557
I'm glad everyone's okay, but we
really can't do that right now, sorry.

305
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:20,934
Fair enough, but could you relocate us?

306
00:19:21,260 --> 00:19:25,300
It's kind of nerve-wracking in here
with them around. What's wrong?

307
00:19:25,520 --> 00:19:27,638
Are you guys afraid of the Seraphim?

308
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:30,557
They're supposed to be on the same
side as you guys, aren't they?

309
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:33,280
And now, what if they go berserk?

310
00:19:33,700 --> 00:19:36,406
Hey, there's nothing to
worry about, is there?

311
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:37,720
No, they're safe.

312
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,777
Those bubble balls are
made of the same material

313
00:19:40,860 --> 00:19:43,560
as the Pacifista Mark
III's bubble shields.

314
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:47,100
They're resilient enough
to deflect cannon blasts.

315
00:19:47,580 --> 00:19:50,160
They're also created with sea energy,

316
00:19:50,600 --> 00:19:54,835
making them the perfect prison to
contain those with Devil Fruit powers.

317
00:19:55,220 --> 00:19:57,920
Oh, I thought they were
just regular bubbles.

318
00:19:58,780 --> 00:20:01,133
How dare you trap me in this damn thing?

319
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:04,317
It is foolish to be afraid of us!

320
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:08,800
We do our job and none of the
Seraphim were ordered to kill you.

321
00:20:08,940 --> 00:20:10,680
You're of no interest to us

322
00:20:11,380 --> 00:20:12,210
Then

323
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:14,480
Now I just feel silly?

324
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:17,100
Don't buy the suits, Snake.

325
00:20:17,280 --> 00:20:18,217
They're just chomping.

326
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:20,997
You're super cool in our book
after what you did before

327
00:20:21,080 --> 00:20:24,139
Thanks for turning us back
from stone little sister.

328
00:20:24,340 --> 00:20:25,677
She really did that?

329
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:27,340
How peculiar.

330
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:31,836
Unless I made an error, that behavior
should not be in the programming.

331
00:20:33,500 --> 00:20:35,360
Come on! Please, Hancock!

332
00:20:35,620 --> 00:20:36,738
They're my friends!

333
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:39,353
You've got to undo this stone thing now!

334
00:20:39,440 --> 00:20:42,580
You're the only person who
can save them, so please!

335
00:20:46,340 --> 00:20:47,357
Alright, fine!

336
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:48,560
I'll undo it!

337
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:51,252
Just please stop staring at me like that!

338
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:53,637
Oh, I see how it is.

339
00:20:53,720 --> 00:20:57,080
She's just as unmanageable
as the original Hancock,

340
00:20:57,300 --> 00:20:59,300
with the same soft spot for Luffy.

341
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:00,580
This is too funny.

342
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,070
Ooh.

343
00:21:02,340 --> 00:21:04,780
I didn't know Seraphim worked that way.

344
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:06,400
Oh, hi, Hancock.

345
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:08,380
How's it going?

346
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:10,537
It seems the information
transmitted through

347
00:21:10,620 --> 00:21:13,197
bloodline elements is
broader than I thought.

348
00:21:13,280 --> 00:21:14,110
Fascinating.

349
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:16,500
You were super awesome back there.

350
00:21:16,660 --> 00:21:17,520
I owe you.

351
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:19,000
I owe you.

352
00:21:19,180 --> 00:21:20,420
I owe you.

353
00:21:20,700 --> 00:21:22,500
I owe you. What? What?

354
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:24,520
Did you just say I love you?

355
00:21:31,360 --> 00:21:33,200
Hey, Stella, we've got trouble.

356
00:21:33,580 --> 00:21:36,345
The communication system's
been fully restored,

357
00:21:36,560 --> 00:21:39,795
but the Frontier Dome still
won't open for some reason.

358
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,440
Don't even bother.

359
00:21:43,080 --> 00:21:45,260
I protected the dome with a passcode,

360
00:21:45,420 --> 00:21:48,361
but my brain's not synced
with all of you anymore.

361
00:21:48,520 --> 00:21:49,677
And I'm not telling!

362
00:21:49,760 --> 00:21:50,680
Oh, yeah!

363
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:53,840
And I beat it out of your bed!

364
00:21:54,340 --> 00:21:55,180
Lilith, no!

365
00:21:58,040 --> 00:22:01,216
While all of you lose your
minds, I'm gonna rest easy.

366
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:03,540
Now, go fetch me a snack.

367
00:22:04,380 --> 00:22:06,262
Snap on my fists, you big fists!

368
00:22:06,380 --> 00:22:09,556
If we can't deactivate the
bed, then we hopped escape.

369
00:22:10,140 --> 00:22:12,957
After all my smooth tucking,
I thought we were free.

370
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:14,746
Yeah, you're a real diplomat.

371
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:27,537
or seriously injured two of
agapunk satellites dead as for the

372
00:22:27,620 --> 00:22:34,300
Straw Hats you're mumbling what's
wrong just talking to myself

373
00:22:37,040 --> 00:22:40,922
i checked outside and were completely
surrounded in all directions

374
00:22:41,900 --> 00:22:48,020
hello Stussy it looks like 100 ships i'd
assume there are around 30 000 marines

375
00:22:48,760 --> 00:22:50,660
My, this is quite the event.

376
00:22:50,940 --> 00:22:52,720
Welcome back, my darling.

377
00:22:53,380 --> 00:22:54,920
Care for a cup of coffee?

378
00:22:55,340 --> 00:22:56,420
Why, thank you.

379
00:22:58,300 --> 00:22:59,700
Stop glaring at me.

380
00:23:00,240 --> 00:23:01,475
You're Nami, correct?

381
00:23:01,720 --> 00:23:03,020
The cruise navigator?

382
00:23:03,300 --> 00:23:04,520
Uh-huh, that's me.

383
00:23:04,980 --> 00:23:06,940
How does a route look? Uh,

384
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:12,282
the log post hasn't recorded a signal, but
we still have one steady needle from 1L.

385
00:23:12,540 --> 00:23:14,364
Seems we'll be going northeast.

386
00:23:14,720 --> 00:23:16,220
Ah, that would be Elbaf.

387
00:23:16,460 --> 00:23:17,600
Elbaf, really?

388
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:20,400
We're going! Finally!

389
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,180
Guess so, yeah.

390
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:23,760
And what's there?

391
00:23:26,060 --> 00:23:27,340
The Giants!

392
00:23:28,860 --> 00:23:30,140
The Giants!

393
00:23:30,520 --> 00:23:31,880
The Giants!

394
00:23:32,040 --> 00:23:34,400
Why are they so excited about this?

395
00:23:37,340 --> 00:23:39,280
We do have one advantage.

396
00:23:39,700 --> 00:23:43,200
Your ship is up here in the
Lobby phase within our grasp.

397
00:23:43,500 --> 00:23:46,097
The Navy ships are
offshore in all directions.

398
00:23:46,180 --> 00:23:49,180
It would be impossible
to sail out to the port.

399
00:23:49,720 --> 00:23:52,237
You said that we'll be
heading to the northeast.

400
00:23:52,320 --> 00:23:54,440
That's the back side of the island.

401
00:23:54,980 --> 00:23:58,657
Luckily, your ship is waiting
right next to the Vega Force One.

402
00:23:58,740 --> 00:24:00,617
With a little rocket propulsion,

403
00:24:00,700 --> 00:24:04,017
it should be able to carry us
clean over the Navy blockade.

404
00:24:04,100 --> 00:24:08,617
On the downside, Vega Force One can only
fly within the airspace over Egghead.

405
00:24:08,700 --> 00:24:11,697
So let's hope we get enough distance
before we take a north dive.

406
00:24:11,780 --> 00:24:13,737
There's no way that'll be far enough.

407
00:24:13,820 --> 00:24:14,717
I gotcha, Zack.

408
00:24:14,800 --> 00:24:15,630
Doc,

409
00:24:15,713 --> 00:24:16,657
you just do the best you can,

410
00:24:16,740 --> 00:24:19,597
then the Sunnies coup de burst
will carry us the rest of the way.

411
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:21,380
We'll fly a whole kilometer.

412
00:24:21,680 --> 00:24:23,737
No way they'll catch us after that.

413
00:24:23,820 --> 00:24:24,660
My goodness.

414
00:24:25,040 --> 00:24:27,511
How in the world can your ship fly so far?

415
00:24:27,680 --> 00:24:29,480
Cool-a-power, Vegapro.

416
00:24:29,820 --> 00:24:30,920
Cool-a-power?

417
00:24:39,760 --> 00:24:40,920
I love it.

418
00:24:41,060 --> 00:24:42,472
That sounds like a plan.

419
00:24:42,660 --> 00:24:43,490
Ah, yeah.

420
00:24:44,840 --> 00:24:46,940
Can you head to Vega Force One now?

421
00:24:47,180 --> 00:24:48,457
I know what you're thinking.

422
00:24:48,540 --> 00:24:52,097
You want me to move the Straw Hat's ship
to the backside of the island, right?

423
00:24:52,180 --> 00:24:53,200
I'll help, too.

424
00:24:53,480 --> 00:24:57,237
But we still can't go anywhere till
we deactivate the darn Frontier Dome.

425
00:24:57,320 --> 00:24:59,614
And I'm never gonna hand over the code.

426
00:25:07,440 --> 00:25:08,540
We'll crack it!

427
00:25:08,660 --> 00:25:10,072
We'll crack the pumpkin!

428
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:15,077
Seems like our plan is
coming together nicely.

429
00:25:15,160 --> 00:25:19,278
I bet there's absolutely zero chance
we pull this off without a hitch.

430
00:25:20,200 --> 00:25:21,259
That's all we got.

431
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:23,029
We don't know till we try.

432
00:25:23,280 --> 00:25:24,820
Yeah, that's true enough.

433
00:25:25,420 --> 00:25:27,217
If you're going to the city, take me with.

434
00:25:27,300 --> 00:25:30,040
That is my baby after all. Take me too!

435
00:25:30,480 --> 00:25:32,237
I can't wait to see Elbow!

436
00:25:32,320 --> 00:25:33,680
Hey, let me help out!

437
00:25:34,980 --> 00:25:36,220
Oh, so cute.

438
00:25:38,720 --> 00:25:39,550
Ready?

439
00:25:46,520 --> 00:25:47,880
Full speed ahead!

440
00:25:48,140 --> 00:25:49,081
It's time to go!

441
00:25:57,180 --> 00:25:59,377
Let's get your ship to
the backside, quick.

442
00:25:59,460 --> 00:26:01,857
Knowing them, they'll have
that frontier dome down soon.

443
00:26:01,940 --> 00:26:04,737
That might be good, or it might
just cause even more problems.

444
00:26:04,820 --> 00:26:05,702
I don't get it.

445
00:26:05,800 --> 00:26:07,297
Why wouldn't you want it down?

446
00:26:07,380 --> 00:26:08,517
Because there's a catch.

447
00:26:08,600 --> 00:26:10,757
If we can get out, the feds can get in.

448
00:26:10,840 --> 00:26:13,917
If we're not ready to rock when
it opens, we're in trouble.

449
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:15,580
Oh, I see now.

450
00:26:15,900 --> 00:26:17,080
This is so much fun.

451
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:18,812
I've never left Egghead.

452
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:20,118
World, here I come.

453
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:22,416
Come on, Doc, this ain't a road trip.

454
00:26:23,120 --> 00:26:24,767
I just thought of something.

455
00:26:26,320 --> 00:26:28,379
We're gonna need so much more food.

456
00:26:28,540 --> 00:26:29,597
Oh, yeah, you're right.

457
00:26:29,680 --> 00:26:31,217
We'll eat all of this in one day.

458
00:26:31,300 --> 00:26:32,257
Do we even have pizzas?

459
00:26:32,340 --> 00:26:33,917
Crap, that's super important.

460
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:35,517
We have to get a ton of cheese.

461
00:26:35,600 --> 00:26:38,717
I think we have everything else
Sanji needs to make them for us.

462
00:26:38,800 --> 00:26:39,630
Really?

463
00:26:40,040 --> 00:26:41,687
That guy's pretty cool, huh?

464
00:26:41,800 --> 00:26:43,918
He's a good cook and a good fighter.

465
00:26:44,660 --> 00:26:45,820
Huh, this is weird.

466
00:26:46,100 --> 00:26:49,057
What's got you in such a
happy mood all of a sudden?

467
00:26:49,140 --> 00:26:51,552
Earlier you wanted to kill old man Apple.

468
00:26:56,980 --> 00:26:58,400
You're right, I did.

469
00:26:58,600 --> 00:26:59,894
But I'm over that now.

470
00:27:01,760 --> 00:27:02,590
That's good.

471
00:27:02,673 --> 00:27:04,917
So why were you crying all night?

472
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:10,217
We've received a transmission from Lucci.

473
00:27:10,300 --> 00:27:12,577
We know the situation inside the dome.

474
00:27:12,660 --> 00:27:18,197
Now share it with the other ships.

475
00:27:18,280 --> 00:27:19,320
Yes sir.

476
00:27:25,920 --> 00:27:28,240
Did you hear that, Borsalino?

477
00:27:29,540 --> 00:27:30,370
Uh-huh.

478
00:27:31,360 --> 00:27:32,497
He talked a big game,

479
00:27:32,580 --> 00:27:35,997
but it seems he doesn't have quite
as much leverage as he implied.

480
00:27:36,080 --> 00:27:39,840
In fact, all of them are
trapped in that dome like rats.

481
00:27:40,020 --> 00:27:44,440
If it uses a laser defense system,
can't you simply pass through it?

482
00:27:44,560 --> 00:27:47,297
You are like itself, are you not?

483
00:27:47,380 --> 00:27:49,909
Well, the barrier isn't
what's stopping me.

484
00:27:50,120 --> 00:27:51,717
There's a friend of mine waiting on the

485
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:54,506
shore and he's determined
to protect Vegapunk.

486
00:27:54,600 --> 00:27:56,380
Why not fly over him?

487
00:27:56,640 --> 00:27:59,957
I can't disrespect a man who's
putting everything on the line.

488
00:28:00,040 --> 00:28:02,216
I like to think I'm cooler than that.

489
00:28:02,500 --> 00:28:05,382
At the very least, let me
stick to my principles.

490
00:28:06,200 --> 00:28:07,160
And remember,

491
00:28:07,540 --> 00:28:09,417
since Amaru is poised to attack,

492
00:28:09,500 --> 00:28:13,277
the second we make a move he'll order
every resource at his command into action.

493
00:28:13,360 --> 00:28:17,480
That means a swarm of sea beast
weapons and 50 Pacifistas.

494
00:28:17,640 --> 00:28:19,875
Bad news for all the ships we brought.

495
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:22,940
We'll be committing to
a massive bloodbath.

496
00:28:24,920 --> 00:28:26,900
We better settle this quickly.

497
00:28:27,820 --> 00:28:30,280
Do we know where the power plant is?

498
00:28:34,460 --> 00:28:37,342
Our friend Lucci hasn't
been sleeping on the job.

499
00:28:38,300 --> 00:28:42,888
We have all the information we need, and
he delivered it straight to our door.

500
00:28:59,440 --> 00:29:03,340
Six Power Masters, proceed to
land as soon as the battle begins!

501
00:29:03,600 --> 00:29:06,780
Our mission is to free the
captured cyberbull agents!

502
00:29:07,700 --> 00:29:10,257
Artillery fire won't
work on the pacifesians!

503
00:29:10,340 --> 00:29:14,160
AIM ALL CANDONS AT THE
SEAT-RAISED WEAPONS!

504
00:29:24,160 --> 00:29:26,240
It sure is fine!

505
00:29:26,740 --> 00:29:28,500
Just like on Sky Island!

506
00:29:30,460 --> 00:29:33,580
I love this place too,
but we gotta lock it!

507
00:29:35,780 --> 00:29:37,720
Made it! Where's the Sunny?

508
00:29:47,260 --> 00:29:49,260
No turning back.

509
00:29:49,900 --> 00:29:52,260
Secret Yata Mirror.

510
00:30:10,340 --> 00:30:12,860
What the? He's here. Let's go!

511
00:30:13,920 --> 00:30:14,750
Pacifistas!

512
00:30:30,540 --> 00:30:32,880
I won't go easy on you!

513
00:30:33,720 --> 00:30:34,550
Simplomaru!

514
00:30:36,660 --> 00:30:38,860
Bring it on, uncle!

515
00:30:40,340 --> 00:30:46,660
You're facing the strongest
defense in the whole world!

516
00:30:57,140 --> 00:30:57,970
What?

517
00:30:58,053 --> 00:30:59,200
What's going on?

518
00:30:59,560 --> 00:31:01,442
Where is this light coming from?

519
00:31:05,120 --> 00:31:06,300
Someone's here!

520
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:09,120
Someone's strong!

521
00:31:42,340 --> 00:31:44,580
Thank you.

522
00:32:17,120 --> 00:32:19,920
Thank you.
